## Adding local Lmod modules to OpenHPC hierarchy

Administrators may wish to add locally built software packages to the OpenHPC
module hierarchy. This can be accomplished by creating module files in the
appropriate locations under `/opt/ohpc/pub/moduledeps` or
`/opt/ohpc/pub/modulefiles`. Two sample module files are included in the
`examples-ohpc` package—one representing an application with no compiler or MPI
runtime dependencies, and one dependent on OpenMPI and the GNU toolchain. Simply
copy these files to the prescribed locations, and the `lmod` application should
pick them up automatically.

```bash
# Create a simple example module
mkdir /opt/ohpc/pub/modulefiles/example1
cp /opt/ohpc/pub/examples/example.modulefile \
    /opt/ohpc/pub/modulefiles/example1/1.0

# Create an example module with a dependency
mkdir /opt/ohpc/pub/moduledeps/gnu7-openmpi3/example2
cp /opt/ohpc/pub/examples/example-mpi-dependent.modulefile \
    /opt/ohpc/pub/moduledeps/gnu7-openmpi3/example2/1.0

# Show modules
module avail
```

